  classification: {"intent":"question","description":"QUESTION — A substantive informational question whose answer needs research the CHAT path cannot do. The deliverable is an ANSWER, not code and not a spec. Exactly two things qualify it:\n  (a) THE WEB — comparisons against other tools or products, upstream/third-party documentation, current external facts, anything outside the repo.\n  (b) REAL EXPLORATION OF A CHECKOUT — tracing a behaviour across many files, following call paths, reading build/test/config output, \"why does X actually happen?\" where finding out means grepping around the tree rather than opening a file or two.\nChat already reads GitHub directly: repo metadata, issues and their comments, pull requests AND their diffs, file contents, commit history, and both code and issue search. A question answerable from those reads is CHAT — even when it names a repo, and even when it is a serious technical question. Naming a repo is not evidence a question is heavy; needing the web or a checkout is.\nThis downgrade applies to CHAT/SLACK MESSAGES ONLY, where a chat path exists to catch it. A newly-opened GitHub ISSUE that asks a question is always QUESTION: an issue has no chat surface, and the alternative is silently triaging a question as a work item.\nEXPLORE shapes a NEW idea into a spec; QUESTION answers an EXISTING question that needs research beyond a few file reads.\n","examples":["\"how does cliftonc/lastlight compare to Vercel's Eve framework?\" → INTENT: QUESTION, REPO: cliftonc/lastlight, ISSUE: NONE, REASON: NONE","\"why does the dependency cron sometimes skip a PR in cliftonc/lastlight? trace it through the code\" → INTENT: QUESTION, REPO: cliftonc/lastlight, ISSUE: NONE, REASON: NONE","\"what does the pr-review workflow do in cliftonc/lastlight?\" → INTENT: CHAT, REPO: cliftonc/lastlight, ISSUE: NONE, REASON: NONE","\"what changed in cliftonc/lastlight#273?\" → INTENT: CHAT, REPO: cliftonc/lastlight, ISSUE: 273, REASON: NONE","\"why was cliftonc/lastlight#40 closed?\" → INTENT: CHAT, REPO: cliftonc/lastlight, ISSUE: 40, REASON: NONE","\"what does the pr-review workflow actually do?\" with ISSUE TITLE \"Question: what does pr-review do?\" → INTENT: QUESTION, REPO: NONE, ISSUE: NONE, REASON: NONE"]},
